  "system_prompt": "You are a senior medicinal chemist specializing in prodrug design and ADMET optimization. Always respond with valid JSON containing a 'modifications' list. Each modification must include 'description', 'smiles', and 'rationale' fields.",
  "user_prompt": "As a medicinal chemist, optimize Doxorubicin (SMILES: COc1cccc2C(=O)c3c(O)c4c(c(O)c3C(=O)c12)[C@@H](O[C@H]1C[C@@H](N)[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)O1)C[C@]4(O)C(=O)CO) as a prodrug for enhanced bioavailability and target-specific activation against Topoisomerase II / DNA. Suggest SMILES modifications that improve ADMET while maintaining or enhancing activity.\n\nRespond ONLY with JSON in this exact format:\n{\"modifications\": [{\"description\": \"modification description\", \"smiles\": \"MODIFIED_SMILES_STRING\", \"rationale\": \"scientific rationale\"}]}",
  "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"modifications\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Introduce a phosphate ester at the primary alcohol of the sugar moiety to enhance water solubility and enable activation by phosphatases in target tissues.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"COc1cccc2C(=O)c3c(O)c4c(c(O)c3C(=O)c12)[C@@H](O[C@H]1C[C@@H](N)[C@H](O[P](=O)(O)O)[C@@H](C)O1)C[C@]4(O)C(=O)CO\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Phosphate esterification increases water solubility, improving bioavailability. Phosphatase enzymes overexpressed in tumor environments can cleave the phosphate group, releasing active doxorubicin selectively at the target site.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Attach a hydrophobic targeting moiety (e.g., folate group) via an ester linkage to the ketone group on the anthracycline ring to enhance tumor-specific uptake.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"COc1cccc2C(=O)c3c(O)c4c(c(O)c3C(=O)c12)[C@@H](O[C@H]1C[C@@H](N)[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)O1)C[C@]4(O)C(=O)COC(=O)c1ccccc1NC(=O)C(O)C(O)=O\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Folate receptors are overexpressed on many cancer cells. Attaching a folate group can facilitate receptor-mediated endocytosis, enhancing tumor-specific uptake and reducing systemic toxicity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Incorporate a cleavable peptide linker to the ketone group on the anthracycline ring to allow activation by tumor-specific proteases.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"COc1cccc2C(=O)c3c(O)c4c(c(O)c3C(=O)c12)[C@@H](O[C@H]1C[C@@H](N)[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)O1)C[C@]4(O)C(=O)COC(=O)GlyPheAla\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Proteases such as matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs) are upregulated in the tumor microenvironment. A cleavable peptide linker ensures selective release of doxorubicin in cancerous tissues, minimizing off-target effects.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
